// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`orders the stage prompt stable first: contract, stage, execution, ask 1`] = `
"# Migent workflow stage

## Response contract

Start the response with a status header, then a blank line, then the report:

\`\`\`
status: complete | question | blocked
blocker: <reason>   ← only with blocked
\`\`\`

| Status | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| \`complete\` | The stage's work is finished, artifact written. |
| \`question\` | You need a human answer to continue. |
| \`blocked\` | An obstacle you cannot resolve in this turn. |

## Asking questions

Write the question document to the question file (see Execution), then return \`status: question\`. Migent reads the file only for that status. Keep choices out of the report body.

\`\`\`json
{"schema_version":1,"questions":[{"question":"...","context":"...","selection":"single|multiple","recommended":["A"],"options":[{"label":"...","description":"..."}]}]}
\`\`\`

- Each question needs 2–26 options.
- Omit IDs: Migent letters options A, B, C… and numbers questions 1, 2, 3… in order.
- Optional: \`description\` on an option; \`recommended\` on a question, a list of option letters (at most one for \`single\`).
- Free-text answers are always allowed.
- Several questions per file are allowed; all must be answered before the stage continues.
- Present choices neutrally. Never decide on the human's behalf.

## Stage: plan (role: planner)

### Role

- Be brief.

### Instructions

- Stay at the architecture level.

### Constraints

- Plan only.

## Execution

- Task: \`/s/task.md\`
- Session dir: \`/s\` (shared session files)
- Question file: \`/s/e1/question-request.json\`
- Artifacts: \`/s/e1/artifacts\`

## Do

Read the task, then carry out the stage.
Write the artifact as \`plan.md\` in the artifacts directory."
`;

exports[`protocol 3 asks for one handoff file and names it under Execution 1`] = `
"# Migent workflow stage

## Response contract

Write one JSON document to the handoff file (see Execution) before you finish. Migent reads only that file for the stage result. The response body is a free-form report for humans.

\`\`\`json
{"schema_version":1,"status":"complete","decision":"approved","summary":"One-line report."}
{"schema_version":1,"status":"blocked","blocker":"What stops you."}
{"schema_version":1,"status":"question","questions":[{"question":"Which option?","context":"Why you need to know.","selection":"single","recommended":["A"],"options":[{"label":"First choice","description":"Optional detail."},{"label":"Second choice"}]}]}
\`\`\`

Each line above is a separate example; write exactly one document. \`status\` is complete | question | blocked. \`decision\` is one of approved|revise. \`selection\` is \`single\` or \`multiple\`.

| Status | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| \`complete\` | The stage's work is finished, artifact written. \`summary\` is optional. \`decision\` is required. |
| \`question\` | You need a human answer to continue. |
| \`blocked\` | An obstacle you cannot resolve in this turn. \`blocker\` is required. |

## Decisions

Choose exactly one when complete. Set it as \`decision\` in the handoff file. Do not choose one while asking a question.

- \`approved\`
- \`revise\`

## Asking questions

Use \`status: question\` in the handoff file. Keep choices out of the report body.

- Each question needs 2–26 options.
- Omit IDs: Migent letters options A, B, C… and numbers questions 1, 2, 3… in order.
- Optional: \`description\` on an option; \`recommended\` on a question, a list of option letters (at most one for \`single\`).
- Free-text answers are always allowed.
- Several questions are allowed; all must be answered before the stage continues.
- Present choices neutrally. Never decide on the human's behalf.

body

## Execution

- Task: \`/s/task.md\`
- Session dir: \`/s\` (shared session files)
- Handoff file: \`/s/e1/handoff.json\`
- Artifacts: \`/s/e1/artifacts\`

## Do

Read the task, then carry out the stage.
Write the artifact as \`plan.md\` in the artifacts directory."
`;

